{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake","id":278026,"title":"Dealing with that special snowflake","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-11T02:16:22-07:00","id":278026,"title":"Dealing with that special snowflake","content":"So how do you S.T's deal with that one player that no matter what game system has to be the special snowflake? For example you are running vampire the masquerade and he just has to play a werewolf. Or you are all run of the mill mortal F.B.I agents and she has to have some wonky powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T02:29:15-07:00","id":278032,"title":"","content":"If the concept is interesting and executed well, I don't mind such PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T02:44:12-07:00","id":278037,"title":"","content":"We got the one player rhat always wants to be the &quot;antagonist&quot; of the group. Playing aberrant? They're secretly rhe villian, and have powers that counteract the other pc's to boot. Vampire? Secretly in league with a demon or a mage to take over the princedom. Everybody a cop? Well they are a drug kingpin's kid, and plans to get enough info about the pc's to have hits taken oit on them because...reasons. I normally let a bit of real world slip in there, and let their own mistakes come down on their heads. Shooting at a cop? Oh, thats not a paddling, thats the other pc's loading you with bullets. No god hand saving there. Your super powered bad guy caught with the metaphorical pants down around a super strong guy and no back up plan? Hope you had a back up character...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T07:33:19-07:00","id":278117,"title":"","content":"It depends on the situation. When I'm STing OWoD, which I do most of the time, I straight up forbid PC crossovers. If we're playing VtM the players will be vampires, ghouls and/or mortals. I don't allow PC mages, werewolves or whatever in may games. As for playing rare/extinct splats in the game it goes by a case by case basis. If they have an interesting idea behind their character I might just incorporate it into the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T08:28:22-07:00","id":278152,"title":"","content":"Just curious, I understand ghouls, but how mortals can be viable without some other Vampire perceiving it as Masquerade breach? Personally I think it's more viable to run mortal that gets Embraced soonish anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T11:12:24-07:00","id":278225,"title":"","content":"Well, it's technically a masquerade breach.<br /> Unless the witnesses owe you favors. Or you're popular with the prince or primogen. Or if the witnes thinks you'd be a useful catspaw... or any number of things. The Traditions are more of a guideline for knowing when to bribe, really...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T11:41:08-07:00","id":278260,"title":"","content":"That might be relevant since I decided that one of character's friends is worried why she is not phoning back recently and dropped in the town. He is completely oblivious about the existence of supernatural, though he has sharp mind to notice anything fishy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T14:53:40-07:00","id":278381,"title":"","content":"Make it clear that you are still going to run the story you were planning and that to make it work the PC might get a significantly reduced screen time and limited contact with the other PCs. He is basically the assistant ST who is in charge of one little NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T15:10:11-07:00","id":278415,"title":"","content":"I'm already delegating some stuff for players to handle on their own anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T15:49:39-07:00","id":278430,"title":"","content":"It depends on the player and their ideas, but generally I don't encourage it. I'll take it over with the players and see why they want what they want and if that works for me. I'm not saying never, I'm just asking why.<br /> <br /> I can understand the impulse to do it - playing a vampire isn't so special when everyone else is playing one too - but have also seen it turn into a solo game in the middle of a regular game. Being a bit odd without derailing the whole game is fine, but being totally against the whole feeling of the game isn't.<br /> <br /> If a player does it more often than not, I might put my foot down. This could lead to the player sitting a game out, but if they're that stuck on one idea I really don't want to deal with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T17:16:03-07:00","id":278473,"title":"","content":"I might be on the mean side but if players feel the need for characters that aren't in the scope of the rest of those being played I just tell them that this isn't the type of game we are playing and if they don't like it they should sit out. I'm nice about it but I'm not about to ruin the fun for others at their expense. Fortunately I haven't had this issue arise in over 15 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T18:41:43-07:00","id":278527,"title":"","content":"Player: &quot;I want to play a garu in your Vampire game&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;...Sure&quot;<br /> *Player makes a sheet, the game starts*<br /> Me (to the other players): &quot;Ok, hes your mortal enemy.&quot;<br /> *Combat ensues, player's character is killed. Repeat as necessary*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:31:19-07:00","id":278553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278527#post278527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player: &quot;I want to play a garu in your Vampire game&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;...Sure&quot;<br /> *Player makes a sheet, the game starts*<br /> Me (to the other players): &quot;Ok, hes your mortal enemy.&quot;<br /> *Combat ensues, player's character is killed. Repeat as necessary*</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly this would likely not go quite as planned as the Garou would likely be the last man standing, unless the Vamps were all Elders in which case one of them might be left standing. So if going this antagonistically it will mean a lot of new vampire characters being generated and your game not really moving along, but hey each to his own I guess.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Might as well say my own opinion on this.<br /> I'll take it up with the player and explain the why my current game isn't favorable for such a character and try to come up with a character concept that is more suitable for the game as a whole with the player. No reason in my mind to go the above way and antagonize the player for wanting to play something else for a change. And sometimes I just might and up integrating the players original idea within my plot so that he get's to play what he wants and the rest what they want, were all there to have fun after all. One of my funnest, and not in a gonzo way, and most enjoyable horror/action games had I think 2 Vampires, 1 Changeling, 1 Ghoul and 1 Wraith (not Risen) and it features Mages as NPC's as well after certain incidents drew enough attention to warrant a Technocratic investigation and certain other incidents drew Hermetic attention. But the plot did involve ancient demon awakening, although everyone thought at first it was a Vampiric Elder, and the efforts to try and banish or destroy it for good which ended up involving casting it's reliquary, this was long before DtF though so no demons/earthbound as that book sees them, into the maw of Oblivion so everyone had their chance to be on spotlight.<br /> <br /> But all said and done it depends on whether I have a plot ready and how the players idea could work with that plot or if I'm just improvising and sand boxing in which case almost anything goes as I have no set plot and are more free to come up with situations and excuses for the characters to get together, if I even need them to get together at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Answering the actual topic of the thread. 10-11-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T03:51:36-07:00","id":278714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278527#post278527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player: &quot;I want to play a garu in your Vampire game&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;...Sure&quot;<br /> *Player makes a sheet, the game starts*<br /> Me (to the other players): &quot;Ok, hes your mortal enemy.&quot;<br /> *Combat ensues, player's character is killed. Repeat as necessary*</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent way to foster bad feelings between players, ST and generally not have a very good time at all. I don't reccommend it.<br /> <br /> Instead I would try and explain that this is what the rest of the group all have decided on that we want to play, and your concept seems a bit disruptive. If the person then insists and shows he/she absolutely cannot or will not try to play with the rest of under the rules/setting we've agreed on, well, there's the door, mate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T04:24:21-07:00","id":278736,"title":"","content":"I will speak only about my first hand experience here. My players were delighted when we torpored another player for such long time we removed him effectively from the play. He could have predicted annoying people would get him such treatment, and I did not intervene as GM. Torporing that Gangrel was fun, indeed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T04:44:54-07:00","id":278744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278553#post278553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly this would likely not go quite as planned as the Garou would likely be the last man standing, unless the Vamps were all Elders in which case one of them might be left standing. So if going this antagonistically it will mean a lot of new vampire characters being generated and your game not really moving along, but hey each to his own I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are forgetting that it is not a fair fight. The ST is on the side of the kindred in that case. Translated: I will cheat in the vampire's favor if someone whines and throws a fit to bring a garu into my vampire game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T04:51:07-07:00","id":278747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278714#post278714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an excellent way to foster bad feelings between players, ST and generally not have a very good time at all. I don't reccommend it.<br /> <br /> Instead I would try and explain that this is what the rest of the group all have decided on that we want to play, and your concept seems a bit disruptive. If the person then insists and shows he/she absolutely cannot or will not try to play with the rest of under the rules/setting we've agreed on, well, there's the door, mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about *that guy*. Killing his (its never a her) character is the only thing they understand. This is how the conversation will go with that guy, it always does. They want to play the weird thing that breaks the game. You tell them no, thats not the kind of game your playing. They whine about it. The other players start checking facebook on their phones. You tell him again that its not that type of game, and if you don't like it GTFO, He complains more and points out some minor weirdness you allowed another character (example: an out of clan discipline). You point out that that kind of thing IS in the scope of the game. They call your friendship into question. By now the other players are yelling at them. You say &quot;Fuck it&quot; and let him have it, just so the character will die, and the player will leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T06:43:15-07:00","id":278776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278747#post278747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about *that guy*. Killing his (its never a her) character is the only thing they understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't played with enough females, if you think they are immune to this. And if that is truly the only thing they understand, again, the door's over there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278747#post278747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how the conversation will go with that guy, it always does. They want to play the weird thing that breaks the game. You tell them no, thats not the kind of game your playing. They whine about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, door's over there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278747#post278747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other players start checking facebook on their phones. You tell him again that its not that type of game, and if you don't like it GTFO, He complains more and points out some minor weirdness you allowed another character (example: an out of clan discipline). You point out that that kind of thing IS in the scope of the game. They call your friendship into question. By now the other players are yelling at them. You say &quot;Fuck it&quot; and let him have it, just so the character will die, and the player will leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Calling friendship into question ? Listen bud, I'm not that desperate for friends. Door. There. Use it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T07:16:10-07:00","id":278791,"title":"","content":"I agree if they want to call friendship into question over a game we weren't friends anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T13:30:40-07:00","id":278994,"title":"","content":"My snowflake just waves hand and gives &quot;silent treatment&quot; and tries to screw up game. Example-player didnt like not being special in an Adventure! game...so they randomly tried killing an important npc in middle of convo with another pc. By random, I mean walking into restaurant where convo was going on, pulls out pistols, and aims for head...out. of. Nowhere. Similar situation in NWOD game-snowflake has magic, pc stops them from raising dead due to potential city crushing consequences. Flake goes silent for an hour. Out of nowhere, uses a bunch of spells and tries to kill pc. None of this was in tune with the characters concept, nature, or anything. Simple butthurt. Remedy? Adventure character killed. Nwod character- the pc they attacked killed all of snowflake's retainers, allies, followers, etc...merit points not reimbursed because it was caused by actions, not GM hand waving. Lesson-actions have consequences...and if thats not cool? See door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T14:28:07-07:00","id":279074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278994#post278994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My snowflake just waves hand and gives &quot;silent treatment&quot; and tries to screw up game. Example-player didnt like not being special in an Adventure! game...so they randomly tried killing an important npc in middle of convo with another pc. By random, I mean walking into restaurant where convo was going on, pulls out pistols, and aims for head...out. of. Nowhere. Similar situation in NWOD game-snowflake has magic, pc stops them from raising dead due to potential city crushing consequences. Flake goes silent for an hour. Out of nowhere, uses a bunch of spells and tries to kill pc. None of this was in tune with the characters concept, nature, or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't being a snowflake- that is just an immature person being an asshole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278994#post278994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remedy? Adventure character killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the remedy is to eject them from the game until they learn how to play well with others. Gaming sessions shouldn't have to be crash courses on basic social interaction.<br /> <br /> I have indulged special snowflakes in some of my games, and more often than not, it just leads to more difficulty down the road. I have found that people who want to be super-awesome and different, with kewl powers to boot, generally end up being prima donnas who aren't worth the hassle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:37:22-07:00","id":279190,"title":"","content":"Very true. Sadly, snowflake cant leave group. Sibling is in group, and its a package deal. So when I run, I dont play favorites...at all. By which I mean, you screw up a situation that could be deadly...it usually is. Whn I play, I tend to either have little to do with character (not hard...their characters are usually quiet, outcast types, so not interacting has little consequence) or, because my character types are generally &quot;good guys&quot; I try to reason group into at worst stalemate, and at best shutting down black sheep in the corner's plans to do something weird and crazy. Ever notice that special snowflakes are the ones that always have a &quot;different interpretation&quot; of rules that help them make game, or even system busters? Always for our snowflake...disagrees with as written or as run because their way lets them do &quot;teh awesome&quot; thingz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T05:32:45-07:00","id":279545,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine who I never get to play with anymore was always the special snowflake in a confrontational way.<br /> <br /> So eventually I just accepted it. I knew he was going to be a &quot;secret&quot; badguy (or goodguy, whatever the opposite of the other PCs) and so I would give him space to do it. I would just worry about the rest of the world, and let him fight the other PCs through good roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages - Small pack of Garou, and he wants to play a Tzimice<br /> Mage - Almost always Traditionalists, he wants a (Nephandi which I dont allow for PCs) infernalist Iterator<br /> <br /> Always something like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your choices are basically:<br /> <br /> Talk to him about it.<br /> Try to &quot;shut him down&quot; (which really isnt that fun IMO)<br /> Work with it and let him &quot;play&quot; his concept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:40:47-07:00","id":279867,"title":"","content":"I just don't care. You wanna be a scathatch-kinain Get-kinfolk that survived the embrace to become a kiasyd? Go ahead, we're freaking roleplaying so be who ya wanna be. That said, if they try and min max from an unusual backstory that gets old right quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T11:02:06-07:00","id":279899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sarah RPs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=279867#post279867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't care. You wanna be a scathatch-kinain Get-kinfolk that survived the embrace to become a kiasyd? Go ahead, we're freaking roleplaying so be who ya wanna be. That said, if they try and min max from an unusual backstory that gets old right quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then what do you do ? You already have said anything is fine, now you're going to go back on it ? That's setting yourself up for a whine-fest, right there.<br /> <br /> Point here wasn't if the group as a whole should allow &quot;scathatch-kinain Get-kinfolk that survived the embrace to become a kiasyd&quot; , if that's what everyone wants, that's fine. The issue here is a situation where the group as a whole has agreed to NOT play such things, apart from one particular person. In such a case, it's a problem, and not something you can simply ignore &quot;because roleplaying&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T11:09:05-07:00","id":279907,"title":"","content":"I mean to say, if they do it for fluff then cool. I don't have issues with someone wanting to be rare, I don't like it when they only do it to munchkin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T15:20:37-07:00","id":280195,"title":"","content":"How do I deal with the special little snowflake?<br /> <br /> Cause a heat wave. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically, the same as a lot on here: if it's well executed and doesn't disrupt the game, fine. If it causes tons of problems, let the player work on keeping it alive. If they fail, too bad. If they succeed, good on ya, mate!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:07:13-07:00","id":280407,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I think every troupe\u2019s encountered Special Snowflakes. My troupe called those characters \u201cBeautiful Beautiful Butterflies.\u201d +5 Points if you can guess the movie reference. Anyhoo\u2026<br /> <br /> About three quarters of the Butterflies we encountered (mostly from gamers outside the regular cast) were just disruptive, power-gaming assholes. The other quarter were \u2013 what I think of as \u2013 \u201cunderexpressed core concepts.\u201d With some digging, you can find out what it is the players are trying to get at and help them re-work some of the underlying themes of the concept into something that meshes better with the Chronicle. <br /> <br /> These examples come from \u201cguest stars\u201d into my troupe\u2019s Sabbat game.<br /> <br /> Example One:<br /> Player wanted to bring in a Black Spiral Dancer into the game as a \u201cPack Friend.\u201d I immediately said no, mostly because I didn\u2019t want to deal the whole Umbra shctick (To this day I still retain suspicions of the player plotting a creation of the dreaded A-word). I sat with the player and asked him about his proposed character, on the off chance that the thing fermenting in his head was more than \u201cBadass Werewolf hanging out with weak little vampires.\u201d <br /> <br /> Sadly, that was one of the cornerstones of his character, but he did describe a very cool \u201cHills Have Eyes meets Conan the Barbarian\u201d core concept. So, we worked on the concept. After much discussion (and perhaps one or two death threats) the player, the rest of the troupe, and the ST (at the time, Me) agreed on: A former Bratovich revenant Embraced as a Brujah Antitribu. It was butterfly-y enough that the player was content but we didn\u2019t have to bend the flow of the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Happy Ending: I was nervous that the player *might* be disruptive, but our concept development session \u2013 I think \u2013 really got him in the general mindset of VtM. The character inspired a few story hooks and the troupe was genuinely sad when the player went off to college.<br /> <br /> Epic Happy Ending:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Before the player left, we killed the character. It was a short Chronicle that culminated in a Highlander-esque duel between the character and Smiling Jack. It was a satisfying and appropriately epic end for everyone. RIP Jedediah Bratovich. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Example Two:<br /> Player wanted to bring a Mage into the game. He had the character all planned out and it was a rather interesting concept: a Johr-laden Euthanatos necromancer on the run from his fellows, hiding out with the Pack. I told him I loved the concept, but I had two major reservations. 1. Concerns about crossover rules in general and 2. Knowing the other players, he wouldn\u2019t last more than a few sessions until they took a shovel to his skull. I suggested that he take the concept in the direction of an Embraced (former) Mage. We talked and we came up with the same concept but his new prelude included his Embrace and acceptance in the Pack. We also negotiated giving the character Necromancy (the Bone Path) as an \u201cin-clan\u201d Discipline if he sacrificed a genuine in-clan Discipline. I think he settled on Ravnos Antitribu and the forfeiture of Chimerstry.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Note: I wasn\u2019t overly concerned about the reanimated beasties the Bone Path creates. Compared to the times (multiple) the characters unloaded a garbage truck full of szlatcha, a little zombie action wasn\u2019t going to be terribly disruptive. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> These were the success stories. The few that there are stand out while the others\u2026they\u2019ve been beaten into the dark recesses of my memory, hopefully to never haunt me again. And now the obligatory \u201cYMMV.\u201d</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:23:54-07:00","id":280471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=279190#post279190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true. Sadly, snowflake cant leave group. Sibling is in group, and its a package deal. So when I run, I dont play favorites...at all. By which I mean, you screw up a situation that could be deadly...it usually is. Whn I play, I tend to either have little to do with character (not hard...their characters are usually quiet, outcast types, so not interacting has little consequence) or, because my character types are generally &quot;good guys&quot; I try to reason group into at worst stalemate, and at best shutting down black sheep in the corner's plans to do something weird and crazy. Ever notice that special snowflakes are the ones that always have a &quot;different interpretation&quot; of rules that help them make game, or even system busters? Always for our snowflake...disagrees with as written or as run because their way lets them do &quot;teh awesome&quot; thingz.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's a problem. Ditch him. Even if the sibling goes with. I've dealt with this kind of situation before and its just not worth it.<br /> <br /> Ain't nobody got time for this shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:42:22-07:00","id":280501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=278744#post278744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are forgetting that it is not a fair fight. The ST is on the side of the kindred in that case. Translated: I will cheat in the vampire's favor if someone whines and throws a fit to bring a garu into my vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or you could just say &quot;if you don't want to play a vampire you don't have to play in this game&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:14:23-07:00","id":280711,"title":"","content":"See the problem I've run into this time is snowflake wants to play a member of the Celestial Chorus who is a....(Drum roll)... Satanist. Not a full blown nephani but more nephani light, his reasoning is that since Satanism is a recognized religion he should be allowed to play one. Face meet palm....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:07:28-07:00","id":280769,"title":"","content":"La Veyanism is not about human sacrfices and other traits associated with Hollywood Satanism, so he is probably doing it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:16:25-07:00","id":280774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=280769#post280769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">La Veyanism is not about human sacrfices and other traits associated with Hollywood Satanism, so he is probably doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> I explained to snowflake that he needs to do his homework and sell the idea to me, since snowflake hates homework beyond a wiki article I think it's problem solved unless he goes with his second option of voodoo priest, which I've also included the homework caveat so we will see. He's also the type that since he can role play real well he feels that most of the systems rules don't apply to him and thus he should be given all the powers now. Sadly my snowflake is part of the &quot;group&quot; package....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:43:42-07:00","id":282399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=280711#post280711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the problem I've run into this time is snowflake wants to play a member of the Celestial Chorus who is a....(Drum roll)... Satanist. Not a full blown nephani but more nephani light, his reasoning is that since Satanism is a recognized religion he should be allowed to play one. Face meet palm....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let me play the Devil's Advocate here. Pun intended.<br /> <br /> What's wrong with that? I mean, granted, you haven't told us what Satanism means in this context, and in real life the word covers a wide variety of philosophical and religious practices, but what's wrong with a Satanist Celestial Chorister? Explain it to me like I'm someone whose never heard of Mage before, and tell me why it's a bad concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T10:57:38-07:00","id":282527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=282399#post282399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Let me play the Devil's Advocate here. Pun intended.<br /> <br /> What's wrong with that? I mean, granted, you haven't told us what Satanism means in this context, and in real life the word covers a wide variety of philosophical and religious practices, but what's wrong with a Satanist Celestial Chorister? Explain it to me like I'm someone whose never heard of Mage before, and tell me why it's a bad concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faith isn't a serious component of Satanist belief; indeed, most Satanists (at least of the LaVeyan flavor) don't actually believe in Satan or demons as extant entities, and instead just see such beings as counter-cultural symbols. If you really do believe and have faith in Satan or his brood, well... in WoD, there actually are real demons. Satanists in WoD have the capacity to be actual diablerists and those don't belong among the Celestial Chorus, thematically speaking.<br /> <br /> Edit: on further rumination, I think a Satanist Celestial Chorister would basically have the same reasoning behind it that draws people toward real-world Satanism: it is the Howard Stern of religious belief. It is edgy, purposefully extreme, and is guaranteed to offend your grandparents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-15-2014, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T11:10:19-07:00","id":282538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=282527#post282527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Faith isn't a serious component of Satanist belief; indeed, most Satanists (at least of the LaVeyan flavor) don't actually believe in Satan or demons as extant entities, and instead just see such beings as counter-cultural symbols. If you really do believe and have faith in Satan or his brood, well... in WoD, there actually are real demons. Satanists in WoD have the capacity to be actual diablerists and those don't belong among the Celestial Chorus, thematically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are theistic versions of Satanism that revere Satan as a figure of enlightenment and symbol of human freedom like Prometheus or Lilith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:22:09-07:00","id":282639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=280774#post280774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I explained to snowflake that he needs to do his homework and sell the idea to me, since snowflake hates homework beyond a wiki article I think it's problem solved unless he goes with his second option of voodoo priest, which I've also included the homework caveat so we will see. He's also the type that since he can role play real well he feels that most of the systems rules don't apply to him and thus he should be given all the powers now. Sadly my snowflake is part of the &quot;group&quot; package....</div> </div> </div> </div>No gaming is better than bad gaming. You are not required to play with people you don't like. You can always go online.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:53:58-07:00","id":282670,"title":"","content":"Yeah, going to throw my vote in here for &quot;just say no&quot;. STs need to be practiced (or willing) enough at improv to &quot;just say yes&quot; to most things during the game, even when they bend logic and sense a little bit, as long as they don't hurt group cohesion... but they also need the willpower to say no to things that flat out won't work with the group.<br /> <br /> Saying no to a player's concept is one of the most empowering things you can do for yourself. I don't even recommend negotiating much or trying to nudge them into something that barely fits. Just say &quot;no, this character concept won't work, let's find a different one that will work for you&quot;, or &quot;no, this backstory won't work, how about something more like this&quot;. Remind them that it IS a player's job to collaborate and work together with the other players: keeping the group's chemistry working smoothly shouldn't only be on your head.<br /> <br /> If a player isn't interested in playing well with others, they can go buy VtM:Bloodlines or VtM:Redemption on Steam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T20:39:59-07:00","id":283190,"title":"","content":"New snowflake problem-keeps using actual knowledge in game. Character is average intelligence, and rudimentary academia knowledge. Player is reasonably bright and has college degree. Therefore-character knows everything player knows, and in cases of &quot;how would you know that?&quot; Player simply states-&quot;well I assume A, and we can assume B, and internetz equals C, therefore my character knows about A/B/C because...reasons. ive challeneged openly about &quot;assuming&quot; both in and out of game...the other two gm's in the group let it slide, because again-package deal. We cant afford to lose 2 players since one is moving far away, and our group would then be 5. Loose siblings=3 and no one in our group wants that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T21:35:15-07:00","id":283220,"title":"","content":"MBP, I have a similar problem. One of the players seems to want to use their OOC knowledge of the gaming world to try to accomplish things or else assume things that his character knows nothing about. In response? I change the world. I have toyed around with the idea of docking him XP each time he uses OOC knowledge IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:16:19-07:00","id":283288,"title":"","content":"Require that they be able to do any physical action they try, if they complain say &quot;hey you're doing it with mental stats might as well go the whole way&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T03:56:05-07:00","id":283694,"title":"","content":"Well, that is a bit more tricky situation. Keeping the OOC/IC divide can be challenging for anyone, particularly if they're newer to the hobby. If this is the case, I would suggest cutting quite a bit of slack, with simple reminders when you feel it's being fractured.<br /> <br /> If the player is aware and arguing about it, however, the issue is more severe. I would reccomend simply forcing him to spend exp to increase his intelligence and/or skills to the level appropriate to what he is actually roleplaying out. Until he does so, no exp may be used on other stuff. If he refuses that, well, my finger would start pointing towards the door, again. Refusal to even try to compromise is a sign that a player is trying to bully the ST into gettin his/her will. And, well, I never liked bullies much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T05:16:43-07:00","id":283737,"title":"","content":"Yeah...myself and one other in group have been playing together since 99. The others in group joined around 04-05. Im the youngest at 29. We had a couple others who were 1 year younger than me, and had never really roleplayed, but the bulk of the group met in college, and me and my one buddy when I was in 8th grade and he was a sophmore (friends older brother played-introduced me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T05:19:28-07:00","id":283740,"title":"","content":"Stating age and time gaming to show that, this isnt a new problem...its just that snowflake has been this way for 9 years. It makes my teeth ache when he pulls this garbage, and it seems im the only one willing to say anything at all, but I know it grates the others (even sibling) but they just refuse to object to it or call on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T07:18:36-07:00","id":283832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=283190#post283190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New snowflake problem-keeps using actual knowledge in game. Character is average intelligence, and rudimentary academia knowledge. Player is reasonably bright and has college degree. Therefore-character knows everything player knows, and in cases of &quot;how would you know that?&quot; Player simply states-&quot;well I assume A, and we can assume B, and internetz equals C, therefore my character knows about A/B/C because...reasons. ive challeneged openly about &quot;assuming&quot; both in and out of game...the other two gm's in the group let it slide, because again-package deal. We cant afford to lose 2 players since one is moving far away, and our group would then be 5. Loose siblings=3 and no one in our group wants that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This one is easy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, player, while you are a smart guy and have the proper knowledge to discern that easily... your character has X dots in Intelligence and Y dots in 'appropriate knowledge'. Since you have a pretty well detailed plan of action (A-&gt;B-&gt;C) the difficulty is only Z. Let's see how much he knows.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:45:56-07:00","id":283925,"title":"","content":"If they have a good idea, allow it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise calmly explain to them how what they want to do wouldn't fit into the theme or the mood of your story. Then talk to them about what they want out of their character and make suggestions...try to find a middle ground. <br /> <br /> Maybe the reason they want to play a garou in a vampire game is they really want to play an outsider, one that doesn't feel like they fit into any modern social structure. Get to what they really want, not just what's on their character sheet.<br /> <br /> At this point, if they still push the issue I'll just say 'no'. I've only had one person let it get to this point and she remained mad at me. I reminded her she's getting worked up and stressed out over &quot;play-pretending to be a vampire&quot;. She laughed and it turned out okay.<br /> <br /> Basic people skills 101.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:59:36-07:00","id":283932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darthcoffee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=283925#post283925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She laughed and it turned out okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>You, my friend, lucked out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T11:49:39-07:00","id":284005,"title":"","content":"Half of my group is desperately lacking in basic people skills 101. 2 of them are IT support...effectively they are the Jimmy Fallon IT guy from the SNL skits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:24:54-07:00","id":284135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=283694#post283694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that is a bit more tricky situation. Keeping the OOC/IC divide can be challenging for anyone, particularly if they're newer to the hobby. If this is the case, I would suggest cutting quite a bit of slack, with simple reminders when you feel it's being fractured.<br /> <br /> If the player is aware and arguing about it, however, the issue is more severe. I would reccomend simply forcing him to spend exp to increase his intelligence and/or skills to the level appropriate to what he is actually roleplaying out. Until he does so, no exp may be used on other stuff. If he refuses that, well, my finger would start pointing towards the door, again. Refusal to even try to compromise is a sign that a player is trying to bully the ST into gettin his/her will. And, well, I never liked bullies much.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair there is a STRONGLY held belief among rpers that &quot;If you can't do it mental/social you can't do it&quot; and vice versa. Some people need to be told &quot;yes I am making charisma(manipulation, int etc) and if you don't like it you can try sneaking around, picking locks and beating up hobos&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:27:30-07:00","id":284138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284135#post284135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair there is a STRONGLY held belief among rpers that &quot;If you can't do it mental/social you can't do it&quot; and vice versa. Some people need to be told &quot;yes I am making charisma(manipulation, int etc) and if you don't like it you can try sneaking around, picking locks and beating up hobos&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>YES! This is very importantly true. If I as a player come up with a very stupid plan and I roll WITS+TACTICS (Or whatever) and get a Stupendous number of Successes, either that very stupid plan is actually brilliant or the GM needs to find a way to massage it into being less stupid. Stats exist to empower storytelling, that means that low stats (and failures) empower character failure and high stats (and successes) empower character success, regardless of player capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T14:51:36-07:00","id":284240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284138#post284138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stats exist to empower storytelling, that means that low stats (and failures) empower character failure and high stats (and successes) empower character success, regardless of player capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is true, up to a point. That approach can easily be twisted into using stats as a crutch, a substitute for good roleplaying. Just because you generated a character with tons of INT doesn't mean you are a genius, or can even reasonably portray a facsimile of one. In fact, playing a decidedly brilliant character can be pretty hard. Just throwing some bones and saying 'well, I know what to do because I am smart' is not going to cut it. I am not trying to say that to be an acting snob either... if you roll the dice and expect the GM to tell you how to come up with a sagacious plan, you aren't playing your genius of a character, you are just letting him/her be controlled by someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:21:47-07:00","id":284275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284135#post284135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair there is a STRONGLY held belief among rpers that &quot;If you can't do it mental/social you can't do it&quot; and vice versa. Some people need to be told &quot;yes I am making charisma(manipulation, int etc) and if you don't like it you can try sneaking around, picking locks and beating up hobos&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is bizarre. The very basic idea of playing make-belief is to enable people to do what they otherwise could not. If an introverted person cannot be allowed to live out his or her fantasy of being a charismatic, socially active person, just as much as a 100lb weakling can imagine himself to be Conan, that's not a group I want to be a part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:30:19-07:00","id":284341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284240#post284240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this is true, up to a point. That approach can easily be twisted into using stats as a crutch, a substitute for good roleplaying. Just because you generated a character with tons of INT doesn't mean you are a genius, or can even reasonably portray a facsimile of one. In fact, playing a decidedly brilliant character can be pretty hard. Just throwing some bones and saying 'well, I know what to do because I am smart' is not going to cut it. I am not trying to say that to be an acting snob either... if you roll the dice and expect the GM to tell you how to come up with a sagacious plan, you aren't playing your genius of a character, you are just letting him/her be controlled by someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> gaming is a communal activity. Personally I'm prone to allow &quot;smart&quot; characters to roll for contingencies. They get to decide after the scene goes into action afew &quot;I planned this&quot; based on rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284275#post284275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is bizarre. The very basic idea of playing make-belief is to enable people to do what they otherwise could not. If an introverted person cannot be allowed to live out his or her fantasy of being a charismatic, socially active person, just as much as a 100lb weakling can imagine himself to be Conan, that's not a group I want to be a part of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> John Wick just wrote a friggen blog post on it. Its very annoying. And very prevalent. Sometimes I demand they physically perform feats that their character would since they claim &quot;real rolepayers ignore charisma&quot; one time I demanded someone actually perform magick in Mage. Its not the best way of handling things but sometimes its the only way some people will listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T18:58:38-07:00","id":284498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284341#post284341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I demand they physically perform feats that their character would since they claim &quot;real rolepayers ignore charisma&quot; one time I demanded someone actually perform magick in Mage. Its not the best way of handling things but sometimes its the only way some people will listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a false analogy. I don't demand that my players act out everything the character does, but I do demand some level of thought and effort on their part. If you are going to take a physical action, I need it described. If you are going to use a gift or conduct a ritual, I certainly will want it to be accurately portrayed in-game. If you are coming up with a brilliant plan, I also want that to be fleshed out. It isn't a matter of what a character can or can't do, it is how much a given player is willing to partake in the story and not just phone it in. Doesn't matter if it is social smoozing or a duel to the death. We are telling a story together, with some crunchy bits thrown in to add an element of risk. If they put effort in, if fires my imagination and I can in turn give back to them. It is like a creativity feed-back loop.<br /> <br /> Rolling some dice and doing 8 health levels of damage (and simply describing it as such) is boring. Sinking your fangs into a Wyrm-shit's throat so deep you can feel the vertebra underneath <i>pop</i>... ? Now things are getting interesting; I can work with that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-16-2014, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T19:16:16-07:00","id":284507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=283932#post283932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You, my friend, lucked out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> probably, but i deal with difficult people on a daily basis and found diffusing the situation with humor, not confrontation works out best. Just make sure you're not laughing at them..but more the situation (John Stewart does this brilliantly)<br /> <br /> And to be fair, I often allow a lot, because this is supposed to be fun and there's really no other rule than that. Also, I like to see if the player CAN roleplay that crazy Nagloper. The just better have a good backstory to explain what it's doing in a midwest town and how it doesn't get insta-killed by the camarilla, the technocracy, hunters and werewolfs.<br /> <br /> But this girl...man....she wanted to play a Toreador - black furies abomination, and didn't really understand anything about vampire or werewolf...much less what it means to be an abomination. She just wanted to play a 'feminist art lover'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T22:02:50-07:00","id":284643,"title":"","content":"See, I can get both sides of the discussion here, but if a character has 2 intelligence, and 1 academics or occult, then the player shouldnt be able to &quot;assume&quot; or &quot;deduce&quot; that someone is camarilla based on past experiences of another character. &quot;Well, im assuming he is a ventrue because ventrue are the only ones so snobby about blood.&quot; How could your character know that? &quot;Well I assume that because my character has known a catiff for some time now, as shown by my 1 allies dot, its likely he has informed me about the other clans he has met. That would lead me to assume that the biggest thing about ventrue is their selective palate, and most likely the most well known.&quot; Thats crap, dude. You cant assume that much because of one ally dot. &quot;Whatever...&quot; *hand wave. Later the catiff is killed due to being worthless, and the ally dot is returned and replaced with contacts-vampires. See, now that, is complete and utter bs and only flies because our group cant afford to lose 2 players due to lack of fresh blood (hah! See what I did there?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T06:23:10-07:00","id":284901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284240#post284240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this is true, up to a point. That approach can easily be twisted into using stats as a crutch, a substitute for good roleplaying. Just because you generated a character with tons of INT doesn't mean you are a genius, or can even reasonably portray a facsimile of one. In fact, playing a decidedly brilliant character can be pretty hard. Just throwing some bones and saying 'well, I know what to do because I am smart' is not going to cut it. I am not trying to say that to be an acting snob either... if you roll the dice and expect the GM to tell you how to come up with a sagacious plan, you aren't playing your genius of a character, you are just letting him/her be controlled by someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>You, uh, might want to read the other half of my post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T07:08:32-07:00","id":284928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284643#post284643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I can get both sides of the discussion here, but if a character has 2 intelligence, and 1 academics or occult, then the player shouldnt be able to &quot;assume&quot; or &quot;deduce&quot; that someone is camarilla based on past experiences of another character. &quot;Well, im assuming he is a ventrue because ventrue are the only ones so snobby about blood.&quot; How could your character know that? &quot;Well I assume that because my character has known a catiff for some time now, as shown by my 1 allies dot, its likely he has informed me about the other clans he has met. That would lead me to assume that the biggest thing about ventrue is their selective palate, and most likely the most well known.&quot; Thats crap, dude. You cant assume that much because of one ally dot. &quot;Whatever...&quot; *hand wave. Later the catiff is killed due to being worthless, and the ally dot is returned and replaced with contacts-vampires. See, now that, is complete and utter bs and only flies because our group cant afford to lose 2 players due to lack of fresh blood (hah! See what I did there?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While personally I would probably handle this OOC, perhaps in your situation you want to handle it IC.<br /> <br /> In this case, let him assume the vampire is a ventrue - and make absolutely sure he is wrong. With his stats the way they are in that case, his &quot;knowledge&quot; would be fractured and misleading at best, but he wouldn't know that IC. Instead perhaps it is something or someone pretending to be ventrue.<br /> <br /> OR, you could simple go full rules lawyer mode. Create a sheet for that ally, and then check the HIS stats. Combine this with book based explanations of dot levels, and throw your hands in the air as if to say - it's not my fault, rules are rules. I wouldn't do this but I also would just kick him and his sibling out and look for new players, with no consideration of the drama it might cause. I keep the drama in the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T10:28:22-07:00","id":285109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284643#post284643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I can get both sides of the discussion here, but if a character has 2 intelligence, and 1 academics or occult, then the player shouldnt be able to &quot;assume&quot; or &quot;deduce&quot; that someone is camarilla based on past experiences of another character. &quot;Well, im assuming he is a ventrue because ventrue are the only ones so snobby about blood.&quot; How could your character know that? &quot;Well I assume that because my character has known a catiff for some time now, as shown by my 1 allies dot, its likely he has informed me about the other clans he has met. That would lead me to assume that the biggest thing about ventrue is their selective palate, and most likely the most well known.&quot; Thats crap, dude. You cant assume that much because of one ally dot. &quot;Whatever...&quot; *hand wave. Later the catiff is killed due to being worthless, and the ally dot is returned and replaced with contacts-vampires. See, now that, is complete and utter bs and only flies because our group cant afford to lose 2 players due to lack of fresh blood (hah! See what I did there?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not only is this pretty bad roleplaying, but it's also flat wrong. <br /> <br /> - Any vampire can there's multiple flaws that specifies a type of vitae for feeding (forgot the flaw name).<br /> - For 99% of all Catiff, they're not going to know anything about Kindred society. Most will be abandoned once they are sired. They'll have to fight and scrap their way to be accepted (usually only if they are a seer), and even then, most Kindred are not going to want to talk to them, much less give them a warm introduction. It's much higher in likelyhood that the Catiff would give incorrect, 2nd-hand information about Kindred Society.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T14:21:54-07:00","id":285390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=284498#post284498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a false analogy. I don't demand that my players act out everything the character does, but I do demand some level of thought and effort on their part. If you are going to take a physical action, I need it described. If you are going to use a gift or conduct a ritual, I certainly will want it to be accurately portrayed in-game. If you are coming up with a brilliant plan, I also want that to be fleshed out. It isn't a matter of what a character can or can't do, it is how much a given player is willing to partake in the story and not just phone it in. Doesn't matter if it is social smoozing or a duel to the death. We are telling a story together, with some crunchy bits thrown in to add an element of risk. If they put effort in, if fires my imagination and I can in turn give back to them. It is like a creativity feed-back loop.<br /> <br /> Rolling some dice and doing 8 health levels of damage (and simply describing it as such) is boring. Sinking your fangs into a Wyrm-shit's throat so deep you can feel the vertebra underneath <i>pop</i>... ? Now things are getting interesting; I can work with that...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are misunderstanding me. Someone who's not charismatic who tries and puts points in the stats I'll work with. Same with intelligence(For example letting them retcon in plan stuff midway because their character is smarter). Its the players who play int 1 enigmas zero riddle solvers(using their IRL abilities), or smooth talkers with charisma 1, Manip 1 people who use the banner of &quot;real roleplaying' to hide their blatant metagame cheating.<br /> <br /> That make sense? I don't expect the int 5 character to be played by Steve Hawkings but I do expect the person to try, and I don't expect the charisma 5 person to just &quot;I roll ten dice&quot; I expect them to play the game but I also have a duty as ST to make their points count.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T15:08:51-07:00","id":285446,"title":"","content":"I gotcha now. I seem to have been arguing against the extreme. Although I have had others with high Charisma or Appearance to expect to just let their dice fly and have NPC's (or even PCs!) licking their boots without actually doing anything impressive or remotely interesting, but I see that isn't what you were referring to; validating player's stat choices by cooperating them is helpful and cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T15:49:50-07:00","id":285470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/278026-dealing-with-that-special-snowflake?p=285446#post285446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotcha now. I seem to have been arguing against the extreme. Although I have had others with high Charisma or Appearance to expect to just let their dice fly and have NPC's (or even PCs!) licking their boots without actually doing anything impressive or remotely interesting, but I see that isn't what you were referring to; validating player's stat choices by cooperating them is helpful and cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mind you, I've found afew people who just want to roll the dice who are more shy and want to do better but have no idea how ot be charismatic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T17:02:15-07:00","id":285505,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty okay with people saying &quot;Okay I want to do something with this effect, I have the dots but I'm not sure how to go about it, ST could you give me some ideas?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean...some situations, that's obvious. Like &quot;Okay I have demolitions 1, what do I know how to do&quot; -&gt; &quot;well you could go toss some dynamite at the bridge supports I guess&quot;, &quot;okay I have demolitions 5 what do I know how to do&quot; -&gt; &quot;to do it right you'll want to climb up to here and plant these things there, and time it like so&quot;. If players can ask for those situations, why not let them ask for a good way to bluff past a guard? They don't need a walkthrough specifically, but if a player has a manip 5 character, I'd say it's their right to ask the ST to list out what approaches should come intuitively to their character (&quot;well maybe you could pretend to be someone above them in the chain of command and pull rank, or you could blah blah&quot;). If an expression 5 guy wants to rile up a crowd, then sure the ST can make them outline their speech, but the player should be able to ask for an example of some angles they could take.<br /> <br /> Enigmas is annoying as hell here. If you throw a riddle at a player, you should expect them to solve it, or at least make the final intuitive leap, but that just plain doesn't always work. It still seems wrong to deny stuff to a player that their character really should get. I've had situations where I'd write down increasingly blatant hints and even a full spoiler for a player who rolls well, and let them try their very best before opening hints at their own pace because that seems most fun for the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T17:57:52-07:00","id":286280,"title":"","content":"If you come to me with a snowflake concept, it'd had better be fucking mind blowing to get me to allow it.<br /> <br /> And in the case of some character types (Baali, Waywards, ANYTHING connected to Charnel Houses of Europe), you're going to have to have played with me for a long while and I know that you can behave like an adult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}